# Repository metadata. Nothing in the repository references this file: GitHub and
# Zenodo read it directly, so it is deliberately unreferenced and should not be
# treated as an orphan.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Counting positive rational friezes over (1/N)Z"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Vico
    family-names: Bonfioli
    email: vicobonfioli@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/ElVec1o/vico_counting_friezes"
license: CC-BY-4.0
version: 2.0.0
date-released: "2026-08-16"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21958792
abstract: >-
  Counts of positive rational frieze patterns of width n whose entries lie in
  (1/N)Z, with proved search bounds, a closed form at width four, and the count
  at a prime at width five. Accompanied by a Lean 4 library in which the count
  at a prime is machine-checked from the definition of a frieze itself.
keywords:
  - frieze pattern
  - Conway-Coxeter
  - quiddity cycle
  - enumeration
  - Lean 4
  - formalized mathematics
